OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F404A1786097899
OL,3,CHow do wildfires happen? Experts
OL,4,Cexplain the risks
OL,6,FMr Parish explains that gorse is
OL,7,Fpacked with oils - so when it burns it
OL,8,Fbecomes "like a roman candle", which
OL,9,Fcan result in flames rising to two
OL,10,Fmeters.
OL,12,FAs the gorse gets older, the dry
OL,13,Fmaterial drops to the bottom, which
OL,14,Fthe Exmoor ranger says is a recipe for
OL,15,Fthe "perfect tinder".
OL,17,FHe said: "Even if there's a slight bit
OL,18,Fof ignition at this time of year
OL,19,F(fire) can funnel up".
OL,26,@{D@Apm{D@Fpn
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G4/5
